\f1\fs22 The Elvi guard escorted Sarah and Tony into a jagged crevasse between two crumbling buildings holding each other up. Inside, merrymaking grew louder, the crowd thicker, and the anticipation more gripping. Up ahead in the distance, Sarah saw a shimmering light which, to her, vibrated with a gladiatorial, life-and-death ecstasy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Almost there now.\'92 Lonnie pat Sarah\'92s elbow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alongside, Tony still muttered under his breath, \'91If they show their faces again, I\'92ll \'85\'92 and punched the solar plexus of a ghost in the air.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>They emerged into interrogation-strength lighting and onto a fetid half-kilometre-wide field trampled muddy by a horde of carousing Elvi and Cloudborne. Every third ground floor of the bordering buildings housed a bar where Elvi stood dozens deep in line for refreshment. In places where the crowd thinned out, buskers set their battered, open guitar cases and battery-operated amps, and were performing many of the tunes Sarah had heard in the Ghetto\'92s karaoke bars. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What\'92s going on up there?\'92 Sarah asked Lonnie, as Tony shadow-boxed another sage apparition, and nearly collected the jaw of a Cloudborne.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Lonnie hung her head a little, and fiddled with her jacket tassels. \'91We can all agree on the music, sweetie, but never the lyrics. It\'92s like God\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91God?\'92 Sarah interjected indignantly. \'91Surely, you don\'92t\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Of course not, sugar, but there\'92s a reason the old Grayling warranties warned consumers never to play gospel music within earshot of us \'85 
\f2\i ELVIS units
\f1\i0 .\'92 Lonnie air-quoted the last two words and drizzled them with derision. \'91Anyway, all I\'92m saying is, it\'92s like we have this gift, you see, of channelling divine tunes. But none of us agree on the lyrics. Put a group of buskers or karaoke fans together, and they\'92ll be punching each others rhinestones out within five drinks.\'92\
