\f1\fs22 They all sat. Murmuring around Sarah quietened; those in the know, knew the show was about to\'97\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A bright, harmonious blast of brass struck Sarah\'92s ears and chest. Drums and percussion wove intricate beats under the musical proclamation. Guitars, strings and woodwinds rose out of the currents and layered tendrils of complex, swirling licks and chords. Then, out of the tension, the riff of a tune resolved. All around, the crowd bayed like ecstatic animals; they knew the tune. Then the lights exploded, and took Sarah\'92s spirit to a place where only love and colour existed. The beat drew her back into her tingling exhilarated body as the music entrained the rhythm of her soul and swept her down a white-water rafting ride of overture and melody. By the time the second chorus opened, she was singing with the best of them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony grabbed her and hugged her as he jigged and rocked, the music overflowing his body with happiness. Sarah didn\'92t mind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The first tune ended with the classiest of trashcan endings, inciting the audience to cheer and clap and stamp their feet. Before Sarah regained her breath, heart rate and blood pressure, the band launched the next tune. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The band! It took Sarah a while to register the size of it among the shimmering brass and percussion, the warmly glowing wood instruments, and their own jewel-encrusted costumes. Foiling her attempt to count, more musicians seemed to coalesce from the glittering backdrop. There were Elvi all, as were the back-up singers who, in passages where they had no part to sing, emerged from behind their microphones and joined other performers whose role seemed to consist entirely of proving their prowess in karate.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Side stage, a queue of vocalists snaked behind sound gear, and down the stairs to back-stage. As the first number concluded, a new vocalist walked on stage and succeeded her predecessor.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The acoustics of Graceland were remarkable. Where she and Tony sat, as near as Sarah could estimate as the centre of the space, warmth and resonance caressed every note with subtle and rich reverb. Three songs in, Sarah looked up and about for the first time, and saw the balconies of all the surrounding apartment buildings groaning with the weight of Elvi dancing, lip-syncing and performing their own martial arts moves.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The next song shifted mood. The lights came down. The martial artists stood still and attentive. One of the vocal Elvi stepped forward and began a solo. It was a simple tune, raw in its authenticity, which had Sarah in tears before the first chorus. The prior singers astounded Sarah with their range and consistency, their machismo, their charisma, their athleticism and unbounded energy, and their raw sexual power. Now Sarah heard how rich was the tone, how mastered the tremolo and vibrato, how caressed the warbling and sweet crooning, how expert the architecture of phrasing and the sculpture of breath. She heard the refinement of sensitivity, and the depths of vulnerability.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>For the first time in her life, Sarah felt in a state of grace. \'91
\f2\i Where I\'92ll be free to have an honest heart,
\f1\i0 \'92 she quoted from a French playwright not born of her universe. She felt loved, and knew she was a conduit for love. Unending, ceaseless, infinite love.
